# A try with no catch is a compile error.
#
# A try whose error nothing handles is a try that cannot do anything useful:
# the error would stop the script whether or not the block were there. Flint
# requires the catch, so the mistake is at compile time rather than a silent
# no-op at run time.
#
# `try` with a `catch` that has no binding is fine: see nested_scope.fl.

try {
	print("never printed")
}